1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
A research committee for decisions
that deserve a second opinion.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Choose markets, a return goal,
volatility and drawdown tolerance.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Fit scores measure alignment.
They never override failed risk gates.

4
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:10,000
A synthetic NVDA example fails
the investor’s numerical risk limits.

5
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Sample analytical roles are deterministic.
Actual model calls are labeled separately.

6
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:34,000
The planner revisits challenged cases.
H-MEM retains account-scoped context.

7
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Stress scenarios are explicit assumptions,
not forecasts or probabilities.

8
00:01:48,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Synthetic figures remain labeled.
Source links invite independent verification.

9
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Keep the invalidation condition
beside your own research note.

10
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Reopen the original brief,
review and evidence record.

11
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:46,000
A 40% return goal with tighter risk limits
produces no qualified shortlist here.

12
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:56,000
This sample run used H-MEM.
Model executions keep separate receipts.

13
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Qwen and Nemotron ran through Nightshift.
Zetaris live verification remains pending.

14
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Built by Shivam Gupta
with AI-assisted engineering.

